      "writtenOn": "2026-11-04T21:34:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding a new _ext struct and ioctl number works for now, but it doesn\u0027t scale: the next field would need _EXT2, then _EXT3, each with another ioctl number and another legacy branch in zram_ioctl().\n\nWhat do you think about making struct zram_android_ioc_process_prefetch itself extensible instead, similar to openat2/clone3/sched_setattr (or drm_ioctl() for an ioctl example)? Roughly:\n \n - keep the struct append-only, with its size taken from _IOC_SIZE(cmd)\n - match the ioctl by _IOC_TYPE/_IOC_NR rather than the full cmd, and\n   parse it with copy_struct_from_user()\n - copy back min(usize, ksize) only when _IOC_DIR(cmd) \u0026 _IOC_READ\n\nThat way, existing _IOW(..., 3) users go through the same path as a smaller struct, and future fields can simply be appended.\n\nIt might also be worth adding a flags/reserved field (in, must be 0) and having the kernel return its struct size (out) for feature detection, so we don\u0027t need to bump ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_VERSION for every extension.",
